<title>MEXICO: Zedillo pushes for Mexico pension law delay - report.</title>
<headline>Zedillo pushes for Mexico pension law delay - report.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's President Ernesto Zedillo sent a plan to Congress on Monday that could delay for six months the starting date for the new private pension plans, television programme 24 Horas said.</p>
<p>The programme said the initiative by Zedillo would push the starting date for the private pension plans, known as AFORES, to July 1, 1997.</p>
<p>The programme said that Zedillo asked for the delay to allow for adjustments to the legal and financial system.</p>
<p>The AFORES are scheduled to start doing business on January 1, 1997.</p>
<p>A number of private companies have already announced plans to manage the private pension plans.</p>
<p>-- Mexico City newsroom (525) 728 9559</p>
</text>
